Earpiece F-008: frame log and headless replay mode for the Police-911 PCSX2 fork.
Applies on top of pcsx2-vr.patch. DRAFT: written without a build on 2026-11-02 (Todd's rig
was not touched); the two new files are complete (round 2: no __int128, step waits for
PCSX2's FrameAdvance pause), the PINE.cpp / Counters.cpp / main hunks
show where the calls go and need their context lines checked against the tree when applied.
Build and verify per earpiece RIG_CHECKLIST "F-008".

What it adds (opcodes match earpiece-rig/src/earpiece_rig/pine.py):
- 0x40 MsgFrameLog: every PCSX2 of the fork. Reply u32 n, then n x (u32 g_FrameCount,
  u64 QueryPerformanceCounter in ns, the clock Python's perf_counter_ns reads), the vsyncs
  since the last ask (ring of 1024, ~17 s at 60 Hz; the rig drains it 10x a second).
  g_FrameCount is saved in savestates (rcntFreeze), so a replay loaded from a clip's
  savestate counts on from the same frame the clip recorded.
- 0x42 MsgFrameCount: u32 g_FrameCount now.
- 0x41 MsgReplayStep: only with -earpiece-replay; FAIL otherwise, so Todd's game can never be
  driven by it. Payload 132 bytes: head, left hand, right hand, each u32 buttons, f32 trigger,
  f32 thumb x, f32 thumb y, f32 pos[3], f32 quat[4]. Holds that as the VR input for one frame,
  runs exactly one frame (frame advance), replies u32 g_FrameCount.
- -earpiece-replay <pine port> -earpiece-data <dir>: PINE on that port (never 28011), all
  EmuFolders (settings, sstates, memcards, cache) under <dir>, memory cards disabled, Null GS
  renderer and Null audio (no window to focus), VR camera on through the FakeHead path with the
  pose taken from MsgReplayStep instead of OpenVR (no headset session), starts paused after
  boot and only advances in MsgReplayStep.

